 ts started, default format '%H:%M:%S' with TZ=GMT; a custom format argument overrides the default\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Implement monotonic clock mode (-m) per prd004-ts R5.1-R5.3: use Go's time.Now() which automatically includes a monotonic reading; -m is compatible with all format modes and custom format strings including subsecond extensions; timestamps must not jump backwards\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"Implement relative-time conversion mode (-r) per prd004-ts R6.1-R6.5: scan each input line for syslog ('Jan  5 14:30:00'), ISO-8601 ('2024-01-05T14:30:00.000Z'), RFC 2822 ('16 Jun 94 07:29:35 GMT'), and lastlog ('Mon Jan  5 14:30') timestamp patterns; replace matches with human-readable relative age (e.g. '15m5s ago'); when -r and a format string are both given, convert matched timestamps to the specified strftime format instead; pass through lines with no recognizable timestamp unchanged; -r is mutually exclusive with -i and -s\"\n      - id: R7\n        text: \"Implement exit codes and error handling per prd004-ts R7.1-R7.3: exit 0 on clean EOF; exit non-zero and print usage message to stderr on unrecognized flag or mutually exclusive flag combination (-i with -s, -r with -i, -r with -s)\"\n      - id: R8\n        text: \"Respect TZ environment variable per prd004-ts R8.1-R8.2: use user's TZ for wall-clock timestamp formatting in default and -m modes; force TZ=GMT internally in -i and -s modes for elapsed-time formatting regardless of the user's TZ setting, matching the Perl source behavior\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Go's time.Now() automatically includes a monotonic reading (prd004-ts R5.1). Use time.Now() for both wall-clock and monotonic timestamp sampling. Use time.Since() for elapsed calculations in -i and -s modes. Do not call CLOCK_MONOTONIC via syscall.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"The subsecond extensions %.S, %.s, %.T are ts-specific and have no Go time.Format equivalent (prd004-ts R2.3). Implement a custom strftime-to-Go-format converter that pre-processes the format string, extracts these extensions, calls time.Now() once per line, and splices in the microsecond-formatted values.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"In -i and -s modes, set the TZ environment variable to GMT at startup before any time formatting occurs, matching the Perl source behavior (prd004-ts R8.2, R3.2, R4.2). Use time.LoadLocation and time.In to apply the zone without mutating the global environment when possible; fall back to os.Setenv if necessary.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"cmd/ts reads from stdin only, never from files (prd004-ts non-goals). Use bufio.NewScanner(os.Stdin) with default line-splitting. Do not implement --help or --version beyond a usage string printed to stderr on bad input (prd004-ts non-goals).\"\n      - id: D5\n        text: \"Flag parsing uses the standard flag package. Mutually exclusive flag pairs (-i/-s, -r/-i, -r/-s) are checked after flag.Parse() returns; violations print a usage message to stderr via fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, ...) and call os.Exit with a non-zero status (prd004-ts R3.4, R6.5, R7.2).\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"'echo hello | ./bin/ts' produces exactly one line matching the pattern '<3-letter-month> <1-2-digit-day> <HH:MM:SS> hello' where the timestamp uses the default format '%b %d %H:%M:%S' (prd004-ts AC1)\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"'printf a\\\\nb\\\\nc\\\\n | ./bin/ts -s' produces three lines each prefixed with an HH:MM:SS elapsed timestamp; the elapsed values are non-negative and non-decreasing across lines (prd004-ts AC2)\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"'printf first\\\\nsecond\\\\nthird\\\\n | ./bin/ts -i' produces three lines each prefixed with an HH:MM:SS per-line incremental timestamp\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Empty stdin (immediate EOF via 'true | ./bin/ts') produces no output and exits 0 (prd004-ts AC5)\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"'ts -i -s' prints a message containing 'usage' (case-insensitive) to stderr and exits with a non-zero status (prd004-ts R3.4)\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"'ts -z' (unrecognized flag) prints a usage message to stderr and exits non-zero (prd004-ts R7.2)\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"'go build -o bin/ts ./cmd/ts' succeeds with no compilation errors and produces the binary at bin/ts\"\n      - id: AC8\n        text: \"cmd/ts source compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint when run against cmd/ts/... (prd004-ts AC6)\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"ccbc136f-830d-4c55-a241-1238fc961e39","total_cost_usd":0.6666957499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":73877,"cache_read_input_tokens":15559,"output_tokens":7887,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":73877,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":7887,"cacheReadInputTokens":15559,"cacheCreationInputTokens":73877,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6666957499999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"a6dcef1d-a87e-40bf-a941-5ec8f30cfbff"}
